els estimating PRs are adjusted for age group (18–44, 45–64, and ≥65 years).\"}, {\"loc\": \"table 2\", \"q\": \"Two-sided p-value from the t-distribution comparing prevalence of frequent mental distress by whether or not the person had the health-related characteristic.\"}], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"uncertain_fields\": []}", "type": "text"}]}